<title>SINGAPORE: SembCorp expects to perform better in 1997.</title>
<headline>SembCorp expects to perform better in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>SembCorp said on Thursday it expects to perform better this year although the trading and operating environment will remain competitive.</p>
<p>In a statement accompanying its 1996 results, it said the group was able to sustain its expansion despite difficult shipreapir and engineering markets.</p>
<p>It reported a loss of 25.2 percent for year ended December 31, 1996 to Singapore $30.07 million while turnover rose rose 25.4 percent to S$1.5 billion.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65 870 3080)</p>
